Relevant columns and their potential usage/conditions
• “creative_page_url”: ad’s page URL to be returned in the result set  
• “region_stats”: needs to be flattened; filter on  
  – region_code = ‘HR’  
  – times_shown_availability_date IS NULL  
  – times_shown_lower_bound  > 10000  
  – times_shown_upper_bound < 25000  
  also provides first_shown / last_shown dates and the lower‑/upper‑bound impressions  
• “disapproval”: flattened to extract removal_reason and violation_category  
• “audience_selection_approach_info”: check that at least one of the keys  
  (“demographic_info”, “geo_location”, “contextual_signals”, “customer_lists”, “topics_of_interest”) ≠ ‘CRITERIA_NOT_USED’  
• “GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER.REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS”: only table that contains all the required fields  

-------------------------------------------------
10 exploratory‑to‑final Snowflake SQL queries  
(Every query is limited to 20 rows so you can inspect the data step‑by‑step.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick look at removed ads – just the URLs
SELECT 
    "creative_page_url"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect raw “region_stats” JSON for a few rows
SELECT 
    "creative_page_url",
    "region_stats"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Flatten “region_stats” to view fields inside it
SELECT 
    t."creative_page_url",
    rs.value AS "region_stats_object"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."region_stats") rs
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Show first/last shown, region_code and impression bounds after flattening
SELECT 
    t."creative_page_url",
    rs.value:"region_code"::STRING              AS "region_code",
    rs.value:"first_shown"::DATE               AS "first_shown",
    rs.value:"last_shown"::DATE                AS "last_shown",
    rs.value:"times_shown_lower_bound"::NUMBER AS "lower_bnd",
    rs.value:"times_shown_upper_bound"::NUMBER AS "upper_bnd",
    rs.value:"times_shown_availability_date"   AS "availability_date"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."region_stats") rs
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Keep only Croatia (‘HR’) rows
SELECT 
    t."creative_page_url",
    rs.value:"region_code"::STRING AS "region_code",
    rs.value:"first_shown"::DATE  AS "first_shown",
    rs.value:"last_shown"::DATE   AS "last_shown"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."region_stats") rs
WHERE rs.value:"region_code" = 'HR'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Croatia rows where impression counts are between 10k and 25k
SELECT 
    t."creative_page_url",
    rs.value:"times_shown_lower_bound"::NUMBER AS "lower_bnd",
    rs.value:"times_shown_upper_bound"::NUMBER AS "upper_bnd"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."region_stats") rs
WHERE rs.value:"region_code"              = 'HR'
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_lower_bound"::NUMBER > 10000
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_upper_bound"::NUMBER < 25000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Same as #6 but make sure times_shown_availability_date is NULL
SELECT 
    t."creative_page_url",
    rs.value:"times_shown_availability_date"   AS "availability_date"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."region_stats") rs
WHERE rs.value:"region_code"                    = 'HR'
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_lower_bound"::NUMBER > 10000
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_upper_bound"::NUMBER < 25000
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_availability_date" IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Peek into audience_selection_approach_info to understand its values
SELECT 
    "creative_page_url",
    "audience_selection_approach_info"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Filter rows that use at least one non‑unused audience approach
SELECT 
    "creative_page_url",
    "audience_selection_approach_info":"demographic_info"::STRING      AS "demographic_info",
    "audience_selection_approach_info":"geo_location"::STRING          AS "geo_location",
    "audience_selection_approach_info":"contextual_signals"::STRING    AS "contextual_signals",
    "audience_selection_approach_info":"customer_lists"::STRING        AS "customer_lists",
    "audience_selection_approach_info":"topics_of_interest"::STRING    AS "topics_of_interest"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS"
WHERE (
       "audience_selection_approach_info":"demographic_info"     <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
    OR "audience_selection_approach_info":"geo_location"         <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
    OR "audience_selection_approach_info":"contextual_signals"   <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
    OR "audience_selection_approach_info":"customer_lists"       <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
    OR "audience_selection_approach_info":"topics_of_interest"   <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL – five most‑recently removed HR ads that satisfy *all* conditions
SELECT  
    t."creative_page_url"                                             AS "page_url",
    rs.value:"first_shown"::DATE                                      AS "first_shown",
    rs.value:"last_shown"::DATE                                       AS "last_shown",
    d.value:"reason"::STRING                                          AS "removal_reason",
    d.value:"violation_category"::STRING                              AS "violation_category",
    rs.value:"times_shown_lower_bound"::NUMBER                        AS "times_shown_lower_bound",
    rs.value:"times_shown_upper_bound"::NUMBER                        AS "times_shown_upper_bound"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS" t
     ,LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."region_stats") rs
     ,LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."disapproval")  d
WHERE rs.value:"region_code"                    = 'HR'
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_availability_date" IS NULL
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_lower_bound"::NUMBER > 10000
  AND rs.value:"times_shown_upper_bound"::NUMBER < 25000
  AND (
       t."audience_selection_approach_info":"demographic_info"     <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
    OR t."audience_selection_approach_info":"geo_location"         <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
    OR t."audience_selection_approach_info":"contextual_signals"   <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
    OR t."audience_selection_approach_info":"customer_lists"       <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
    OR t."audience_selection_approach_info":"topics_of_interest"   <> 'CRITERIA_NOT_USED'
  )
ORDER BY rs.value:"last_shown"::DATE DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries progress from simple inspection to the fully‑filtered answer query (query #10) that yields the information requested for the five most recently removed ads in Croatia.
