Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage/conditions
• “creative_page_url”: ad’s page URL to be returned in the result set  
• “region_stats”: needs to be flattened; filter on  
  – region_code = ‘HR’  
  – times_shown_availability_date IS NULL  
  – times_shown_lower_bound  > 10000  
  – times_shown_upper_bound < 25000  
  also provides first_shown / last_shown dates and the lower‑/upper‑bound impressions  
• “disapproval”: flattened to extract removal_reason and violation_category  
• “audience_selection_approach_info”: check that at least one of the keys  
  (“demographic_info”, “geo_location”, “contextual_signals”, “customer_lists”, “topics_of_interest”) ≠ ‘CRITERIA_NOT_USED’  
• “GOOGLE_ADS.GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER.REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS”: only table that contains all the required fields  

-------------------------------------------------
10 exploratory‑to‑final Snowflake SQL queries  
(Every query is limited to 20 rows so you can inspect the data step‑by‑step.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick look at removed ads – just the URLs
SELECT 
    "creative_page_url"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect raw “region_stats” JSON for a few rows
SELECT 
    "creative_page_url",
    "region_stats"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Flatten “region_stats” to view fields inside it
SELECT 
    t."creative_page_url",
    rs.value AS "region_stats_object"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."region_stats") rs
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Show first/last shown, region_code and impression bounds after flattening
SELECT 
    t."creative_page_url",
    rs.value:"region_code"::STRING              AS "region_code",
    rs.value:"first_shown"::DATE               AS "first_shown",
    rs.value:"last_shown"::DATE                AS "last_shown",
    rs.value:"times_shown_lower_bound"::NUMBER AS "lower_bnd",
    rs.value:"times_shown_upper_bound"::NUMBER AS "upper_bnd",
    rs.value:"times_shown_availability_date"   AS "availability_date"
FROM "GOOGLE_ADS"."GOOGLE_ADS_TRANSPARENCY_CENTER"."REMOVED_CREATIVE_STATS" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN (input => t."region_stats") rs
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Keep only Croatia (‘HR’) rows
SELECT 
    t."creative_page_url",
    rs.value:"region_code"::STRING AS "region_code",
    rs.value:"first_shown"::DATE  AS "first_shown",
    rs.value:"last_shown"::DATE   AS "last_shown"
